HowNet Simplified Sentiment Lexicon — License and Attribution
================================================================

These lexicon files (`hownet_simplified.pos.txt`, `hownet_simplified.neg.txt`)
are derived from the OpenHowNet project (https://github.com/thunlp/THU-OpenHowNet)
maintained by the Natural Language Processing Lab at Tsinghua University (THUNLP).

Original work: HowNet / 知网 — Dong Zhendong (董振东) & Dong Qiang (董强).
OpenHowNet release: CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

This curated subset was assembled for the yuqing (舆情监控) backend's
JiebaNlpProvider. It includes:
  - a base word list derived from the upstream HowNet simplified sentiment set
  - domain-specific additions for public-opinion monitoring (financial,
    regulatory, consumer-protection, environmental, public-safety vocabulary)
  - filtering of context-ambiguous words whose polarity depends on adjacent
    tokens (e.g. "重大" excluded; downstream hits like "事故/违规/泄露"
    carry the negative signal instead)

You are free to share and adapt the lexicon under CC BY 4.0, provided you
attribute both:
  1. HowNet (董振东, 董强) and OpenHowNet (THUNLP) for the upstream data;
  2. this project (yuqing backend) for the curated subset.

NO WARRANTY. The lexicon is provided "as-is"; sentiment labels are heuristic
and may be wrong for edge cases. The accompanying evaluation pipeline
(backend/scripts/eval_sentiment.py) should be used to measure accuracy on
your domain before relying on it.